{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC precision note (implementation): the four genuine-gap kinds (missing_required_child, no_executable_breakdown, uncertifiable_outcome, certification_cannot_prove) map to contribution 1.0, so impact_plan returns 1.0 for a finding graded only on one of them, not exactly 0.85. 0.85 is the hard-override FLOOR, not a target value; the shipped precedents behave identically (impact_plan({'ac_unverifiable':'missing_oracle'}) == 1.0, and the existing test_missing_and_broken_oracle_keep_the_floor asserts >= 0.85). The AC bullet reads 'each gap kind yields 0.85'; it is satisfied by tests asserting the floor property >= _PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_FLOOR, mirroring the precedent suites, plus a self_revealing case proving the floor survives the 0.8 amplifier. Recorded so the wording is not silently reinterpreted at close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786514669609401001,"uuid":"0b93b55b-41a3-4c9a-8153-9d2fa32b29c3"}